            "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
            "body": "They are defined with `MiniStatuslineModeXxx` highlight groups. Here is a [full list](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/072ef026a538cf4a9dedba56ad8eecffa9e9abb6/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L51-L57). By default they are linked to some built-in highlight groups, which can look not as pretty as you'd expect.\r\n\r\nEither use a color scheme that defines them explicitly (for example, execute `:colorscheme randomhue`) or define them manually (see `:h nvim_set_hl()` and for example of the logic - [how it is done in 'mini.hues'](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/072ef026a538cf4a9dedba56ad8eecffa9e9abb6/lua/mini/hues.lua#L1162-L1167)).",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">They are defined with <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniStatuslineModeXxx</code> highlight groups. Here is a <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/072ef026a538cf4a9dedba56ad8eecffa9e9abb6/doc/mini-statusline.txt#L51-L57\">full list</a>. By default they are linked to some built-in highlight groups, which can look not as pretty as you'd expect.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Either use a color scheme that defines them explicitly (for example, execute <code class=\"notranslate\">:colorscheme randomhue</code>) or define them manually (see <code class=\"notranslate\">:h nvim_set_hl()</code> and for example of the logic - <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/072ef026a538cf4a9dedba56ad8eecffa9e9abb6/lua/mini/hues.lua#L1162-L1167\">how it is done in 'mini.hues'</a>).</p>",
            "bodyText": "They are defined with MiniStatuslineModeXxx highlight groups. Here is a full list. By default they are linked to some built-in highlight groups, which can look not as pretty as you'd expect.\nEither use a color scheme that defines them explicitly (for example, execute :colorscheme randomhue) or define them manually (see :h nvim_set_hl() and for example of the logic - how it is done in 'mini.hues').",
